## 5. File Format & Storage Layout

### 5.1 Directory Structure

```
lattice-store/
├── meta/
│   ├── tree_index.json          # Fractal tree structure
│   ├── domain_clusters.json     # Cluster definitions
│   └── router_state.pt          # Router weights + EWC fisher matrix
├── experts/
│   ├── {cluster_id}/
│   │   ├── {expert_id}.lge      # Lattice-Grow Expert file
│   │   ├── {expert_id}.meta.json
│   │   └── {expert_id}.scales.bin
│   └── ...
├── replay/
│   └── exemplars.db             # SQLite: 1K samples/domain
└── logs/
    └── training_log.jsonl
```

### 5.2 .lge File Format (Lattice-Grow Expert)

```
[MAGIC: 4 bytes "LGEX"]
[VERSION: uint16]
[COMPRESSION_METHOD: uint8]
[BIT_WIDTH: float16]
[TENSOR_COUNT: uint32]
[TENSOR_HEADERS: variable]
  - name_length: uint8
  - name: utf-8
  - shape: uint32[]
  - dtype: uint8
  - offset: uint64
  - compressed_size: uint64
[COMPRESSED_DATA: variable]
[CHECKSUM: CRC32]
```

---

## 6. Benchmark & Validation Plan

### 6.1 Throughput Constancy Test

- Measure tokens/sec at expert counts: 100, 1K, 10K, 100K
- Expected: ±5% variance across all scales
- Hardware: Fixed student laptop (RTX 3060 / 8GB VRAM / 1TB NVMe)

### 6.2 Forgetting Rate Test

- Sequential task protocol (Avalanche benchmark suite)
- Tasks: MNIST → CIFAR → Text classification → Domain-specific QA
- Metric: Backward Transfer (BWT) should be ≥ -0.01 (near-zero forgetting)
- Compare against: EWC, SI, Progressive Nets, standard fine-tuning

### 6.3 Storage Efficiency Test

- Track bytes-per-expert over 10K expert lifecycle
- Expected: ≤1MB average including deltas and metadata
- Compare against: FP16 baseline, INT4 quantization, naive zip

### 6.4 Routing Accuracy Test

- Measure expert retrieval precision@3 over held-out domain queries
- Expected: >85% after 1K experts, >95% after 10K
- Ablation: Hierarchical vs flat routing, EWC vs no-EWC

---

## 7. Open-Source Dependencies

| Component | Library | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| Disk offloading | Colossal-AI | NVMe streaming, pinned memory |
| Continual learning utils | Avalanche | Benchmarks, replay buffers, metrics |
| MoE infrastructure | DeepSpeed | Expert parallelism scaffolding |
| Sub-1-bit quantization | Custom (NanoQuant ref) | Freeze-time compression |
| Delta compression | Custom (ZipLLM ref) | Version-efficient archival |
| Base transformer | HuggingFace Transformers | Working memory backbone |
| Router kNN | FAISS | Fast centroid search |

---

## 8. Known Risks & Mitigations

| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
|------|----------|------------|
| Router fails to retrieve correct expert | High | Hierarchical fallback search; confidence threshold triggers novelty spawn |
| Expert sprawl degrades routing | Medium | Aggressive consolidation; pruning policy |
| Sub-1-bit quality loss in sensitive layers | Medium | Adaptive bit-width; keep attention layers at higher precision |
| SSD wear from frequent writes | Low | Write batching; compress-before-write reduces volume |
| Thermal throttling on old laptops | Low | Gradient checkpointing; batch size auto-scaling |

